From d513a16928b382668c3e64833ad9814fd106545f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:29:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Verify native wallet provider proofs and anchor fences

Exercise the real JSON node provider against disk-generated inclusion and nonmembership proofs, with strict context/proof/frame mutations and typed remote refusals. Compare disk/provider unsigned bytes and verified BIP340 signing meaning without assuming randomized witness bytes match. Inject stale and operational provider outcomes before input resolution, inside ordinary validation and at the final recheck, proving export and reservation fences.

The explicit authenticated disk fixture is copied from eaecdb04b existing wallet tests and does not claim complete-block acceptance. Debug and optimized Release standalone suites both pass the new provider tests and unchanged SQLite/reorg wallet regression suite against engine 4dd1ee357 and adapter 46321a272. Optimized objects link reviewed Debug native archives with mandatory ABC assertions retained; no socket or node end-to-end behavior is claimed. Only four new test/fixture/recipe/evidence files are included.
